heartbeat:
  last_seen: "2026-06-01T18:16:39Z"
  host: "Mac"
  task: "Committed: fix(sync): gate all Firestore saves until startup cloud load completes (isCloudSyncReady)

The core race condition was: renderer fires save-projects with stale disk cache
BEFORE runStartupSequence finishes loading from Firestore. Even with the
lastSyncedProjectIds guard, if saves fire during the startup window they
can corrupt cloud state from another device.

Solution: isCloudSyncReady=false blocks all Firestore saves until:
- runStartupSequence cloud load completes (normal startup), or
- post-auth cloud load completes (mid-session sign-in)

Local disk writes still proceed immediately (for offline cache).
isCloudSyncReady resets to false on sign-out so subsequent sign-ins are safe."
  status: alive
